  {
   "id": "upper-division-engineering",
   "title": "Upper Division Engineering",
   "section": "Upper Division",
   "notes": "EECS has redesigned the power and energy curriculum in EECS to consist of a new introduction-to-power course (ELENG 108, offered every spring), a more advanced power electronics course (ELENG 113, offered every fall), and a new power electronics design lab course (ELENG 113B, offered every spring). In this new curriculum, ELENG 108 is a strict prerequisite for ELENG 113, and ELENG 113 is a strict prerequisite for ELENG 113B. Thus, all students who anticipate taking ELENG 113 must complete ELENG 108.\nELENG 113 and ELENG 137B may not both be used to satisfy this requirement. Students may take one or the other.",
   "rule": {
