  {
   "id": "upper-division-engineering-electives",
   "title": "Upper Division Engineering Electives",
   "section": "Upper Division",
   "notes": "The full text is on the catalog page.",
   "rule": {
    "type": "manual",
    "text": "Complete 4 Engineering electives:\nEngineering electives are upper division courses in any engineering department and must be chosen in consultation with a faculty adviser.\n- Any ENGINEERING course 100-189 (includes: BIOENG, CIVENG, COMPSCI, EECS, ELENG, ENGIN, INDENG, MATSCI, MECENG, NUCENG).\n- STAT 133, 135\n- ENE RES 131\n- COMPSCI 61B\nExclusions:\n- Any course that counts as H/SS\n- Any course less than 3 units\n- BIOENG 100, 153\n- COMPSCI 194-100\n- DESINV courses (except DESINV 190E)\n- ENGIN 125, 157AC, 170 series, 180, 183 series, 185, 187, 195 series … (see the catalog for the rest)",
